   - Update Resource Bundle: PUT /api/v1/bundles/:id (optimistic concurrency control, partial updates)
   - Delete Resource Bundle: DELETE /api/v1/bundles/:id
   - Get Resource Bundle: GET /api/v1/bundles/:id (with caching using Redis or Memcached)
   - Get All Resource Bundles: GET /api/v1/bundles (pagination, sorting, filtering)

2. Optimistic Concurrency Control (Node.js and Python examples):
   - Use a version number or timestamp for each resource bundle.
   - Compare the current version with the expected version sent by the client before making changes.
   - If versions match, update the resource; if not, return a conflict error.

3. External Notification Service (using Node.js example):
   - Implement a listener function to trigger the notification service upon bundle updates (using a library like Nodemailer or Twilio)

4. Third-Party Identity Provider Integration (using Passport.js for Node.js and OAuthlib for Python):
   - Configure your API to use an external identity provider for authentication and authorization.

5. Resource Bundle Loading Function (C example):
   ```c
   #include <stdio.h>
   #include <stdlib.h>
   #include <string.h>

   typedef struct item {
       int id;
       char* value;
   } item_t;

   typedef struct bundle {
       int size;
       item_t* items;
   } bundle_t;

   int load_bundle(const char* path, bundle_t** bundle) {
       FILE* file = fopen(path, "r");
       if (!file) return 1; // error opening file

       fseek(file, 0, SEEK_END);
       long size = ftell(file);
       rewind(file);

       bundle_t* b = (bundle_t*)malloc(sizeof(bundle_t));
       if (!b) {
           fclose(file);
           return 2; // memory allocation error
       }

       b->size = size / sizeof(item_t);
       b->items = (item_t*)malloc(b->size * sizeof(item_t));
       if (!b->items) {
           free(b);
           fclose(file);
           return 3; // memory allocation error
       }

       size_t read = fread(b->items, sizeof(item_t), b->size, file);
       if (read != b->size) {
           free(b->items);
           free(b);
           fclose(file);
           return 4; // read error
       }

       fclose(file);
       *bundle = b;
       return 0; // success
   }
   ```

