[' Here is a high-level architecture design for the `GlobalOrderProcessingEngine`:

```java
public class GlobalOrderProcessingEngine {
    private final Map<String, OrderService> orderServices;
    private final PredictiveLoadBalancer loadBalancer;
    private final MonitoringSystem monitoringSystem;
    private final AutoScaler autoScaler;
    private final RetryStrategy retryStrategy;
    private final FallbackStrategy fallbackStrategy;
    private final QuarantineService quarantineService;

    public GlobalOrderProcessingEngine(
            Map<String, OrderService> orderServices,
            PredictiveLoadBalancer loadBalancer,
            MonitoringSystem monitoringSystem,
            AutoScaler autoScaler,
            RetryStrategy retryStrategy,
            FallbackStrategy fallbackStrategy,
            QuarantineService quarantineService) {
        // Initialize components
    }

    public void processOrder(Order order) {
        OrderService service = loadBalancer.choose(order);
        try {
            service.update(order);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            retryStrategy.retryIfPossible(e);
            if (!fallbackStrategy.canFallback()) {
                quarantineService.quarantine(order);
                monitoringSystem.alert(e);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

The above code outlines the core class for the `GlobalOrderProcessingEngine`, which manages interactions with multiple third-party services through an adaptive load balancer, monitors its performance, and scales horizontally based on traffic patterns. The code is modular, allowing flexibility in configuration for different fulfillment strategies, error handling mechanisms, and monitoring/alerting systems.

